      "updated_at": "2026-10-11T16:16:22Z",
      "body": "Read-only exact-merge review at88966b521. Configuration negative/trained-in multi-seed evidence/count1/3 are retained correctly underD22; do not close H4/E8 or geometric weights. One mathematical/lowering scope needs explicit conditioning: geometric_stack.rs377-399 snaps only weights via host f32/nearest root; params() then expands them with quaternion_dense_weight. Current activations remain general vectors, so a weight-side product is NOT yet a Cayley-table read+shift unless the activation operand is also represented in a closed admitted group/scale form or another exact decomposition is specified. Neither current dense expansion nor weight-only snapping measures table-serving throughput/energy. Separate measured quality of this configuration from proposed10-bit representation and future exact table lowering. Likewise QSf/QSe identifies losses for this tested snap/STE/recipe, not proof that all120-direction learned operators intrinsically require finer codebooks; capacity/training/operand-state contracts remain relevant. The finer exact set is a hypothesis with its own prospective FIT, not a mechanism closure. No peer source/jobs/leases/criteria changed by this audit.",
